# .dockerignore — SEC-37 (OPS-AUDIT-REMEDIATION-LOW-W1)
#
# Without this file, `docker build` sends the ENTIRE repo root to the Docker daemon as build
# context — including the live production `.env` sitting in the deploy directory on the host.
# Nothing in the Dockerfile COPYs it, so it never reached an image layer, but it was transmitted
# to the daemon and written into its build cache on every deploy. That is a live credential
# crossing a boundary it has no reason to cross, and it is free to stop.
#
# ⚠️ THIS FILE CAN BREAK THE BUILD. Excluding a path the Dockerfile COPYs fails the build at
# best, and at worst ships a STALE artifact. The Stage-1 (builder) inputs are the dangerous
# ones, because `RUN npm run build:knowledge` consumes them and their content ships inside
# dist/knowledge/*.json — a silent content regression with a green build. The COPY set was
# enumerated from BOTH Dockerfiles before this file was written:
#
#   src/ · package*.json · tsconfig.json · scripts/build-knowledge-json.mjs · audits/
#   landing/integrations/ · README.md · CHANGELOG.md · landing/Prompt/ · landing/skills.html
#   landing/integrations.html · scripts/fetchers/ · scripts/refresh-knowledge-pages.mjs
#   scripts/funnel-by-channel.mjs
#
# NONE of those may be excluded here. Re-derive the list before adding any rule:
#   grep -hE '^COPY' Dockerfile Dockerfile.facilitator

# ── Key material — the reason this file exists ───────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_ed25519
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.mcpregistry_github_token
.mcpregistry_registry_token

# ── Build noise: rebuilt inside the image, or irrelevant to it ───────────────
node_modules
dist
*.db
*.sqlite
.DS_Store

# ── VCS and local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.smithery
*.mcpb

# ── Test and local-only artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage
.nyc_output
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# NOTE: `audits/`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` and `landing/` are deliberately ABSENT from this
# file. They are Dockerfile COPY sources — `audits/` and `README.md` are Stage-1 inputs to
# `npm run build:knowledge`, so excluding them would ship a stale knowledge bundle rather than
# fail loudly. If you are here to "trim the context further", that is the trap.
